description:
A UUID string in canonical hyphenated form, and it must be a version 4 UUID as defined by RFC 4122 in its variant-1 layout. Concretely:
- 8 hex digits, then a hyphen;
- 4 hex digits, then a hyphen;
- 4 hex digits where the first is '4', then a hyphen;
- 4 hex digits where the first is one of 8, 9, a or b (case-insensitive), then a hyphen;
- 12 hex digits.
Hex digits may be upper or lower case. No braces, urn prefix, or other decorations are allowed.

A single word identifier (also called a slug) is valid when:
- it consists of one or more Unicode letters;
- it is not one of the reserved words "class", "function", "var", "let", "const", "new";
- matching is case-insensitive.

Account password policy:
- length between 12 and 64 characters inclusive;
- at least one lowercase ASCII letter;
- at least one uppercase ASCII letter;
- at least one digit;
- at least one of the following symbols: ! @ # $ % ^ & * ( ) - _ + = ?
- no whitespace anywhere;
- the check is on the whole string.

A ULID must be validated as follows:
- exactly 26 characters;
- Crockford's base32 alphabet, case-insensitive: digits and letters, but the letters I, L, O and U are excluded;
- the first character, which encodes the timestamp, must be between 0 and 7 inclusive;
- all remaining characters may be any Crockford base32 character.

Validate a signed decimal number:
- an optional leading sign, either + or -;
- at least one digit before the decimal point;
- an optional fractional part introduced by a dot and containing one or more digits;
- no other characters, and the whole string must match.
